.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt NVIDIA 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvidia
.Nd NVIDIA GPU kernel driver (native FreeBSD)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd kldload nvidia
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module drives NVIDIA GPUs through NVIDIA's resource manager.
It creates
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl
and one
.Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N
per GPU.
.Pp
The module is native: it has no
.Dv MODULE_DEPEND
on the Linuxulator
.Pq Dv linux , linux64elf , linux_common
and imports no Linux symbol, so it loads and works on a host with no Linux
layer.
.Sh LINUX COMPATIBILITY
Linux binaries (the Linux
.Nm nvidia-smi ,
Linux CUDA, a Linux Vulkan driver) reach the driver through
.Xr nvidia_linux 4 ,
a separate module that belongs to the Linuxulator.
The core only announces its devices:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include "nvidia_bridge.h"

int  nvidia_bridge_register(const struct nvidia_bridge_ops *);
int  nvidia_bridge_unregister(const struct nvidia_bridge_ops *);
.Ed
.Pp
A provider registers a table of two functions,
.Fn nbo_cdev_add
and
.Fn nbo_cdev_del ,
with the interface version
.Dv NVIDIA_BRIDGE_KPI_VERSION
(1) and the size of the table.
The core refuses another version or size
.Pq Er EINVAL ,
and a second provider
.Pq Er EBUSY .
A core built with
.Ev NV_CORE_LINUX_COMPAT
carries the Linux bridge itself and refuses every provider
.Pq Er ENXIO .
On registration the provider is told about the devices that already exist.
The interface is versioned apart from the module: any change to the layout of
either structure raises
.Dv NVIDIA_BRIDGE_KPI_VERSION ,
and there is no compatible extension.
.Pp
Because
.Xr nvidia_linux 4
depends on
.Nm ,
.Nm
cannot be unloaded while the provider is loaded:
.Xr kldunload 8
fails with
.Er EBUSY
and the module stays; unload the provider first.
.Pp
To build the old in-core Linux bridge, which makes
.Nm
depend on the Linuxulator again, build with
.Ev NV_CORE_LINUX_COMPAT Ns = Ns Cm yes .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /dev/nvidiactl
.It Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvidia_drm_render 4 ,
.Xr nvidia_linux 4
